<<
/Title (Driver Only Operation is a 1980s era argument. Governments come and go but unfortunately arguments repeated by the same old railway management are devoid of any new ideas. They are hell bent on wanting to cut corners by de-staffing Trains & Stations. The railways always sell the dream of incorporating new technology but never see it fully though or stabilise the currently available technology. Too often, train operators will ignore practical railway issues by blaming the unions and staff. No matter how much technology advances it will take many years to get full 100% mobile & GPS coverage on the railways due to cuttings, tunnels, viaducts and the many isolated rural areas in Britain.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
